            {
                "entry_id": "92de712e-0021-3d68-b549-706a5aca3b76",
                "word": "MB",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "097cf593-dc24-3794-8541-b4913eb44499",
                        "entry_id": "92de712e-0021-3d68-b549-706a5aca3b76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abbreviation of Manitoba: a province of Canada."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "567aba50-0b12-3034-8fc7-b5fb57b3fcd8",
                        "entry_id": "92de712e-0021-3d68-b549-706a5aca3b76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of Myers–Briggs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f9add6b-a2f1-4f27-815d-30957304baac",
                                "sense_id": "567aba50-0b12-3034-8fc7-b5fb57b3fcd8",
                                "text": "For example, Jung described one type as being introverted sensing. In\nMB terminology, this means that introverted sensing is dominant (ie\nISxJ types). What MB 'adds' is that this function is supported by\nextraverted thinking or feeling as the auxiliary. The mapping between\nthe models is:"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bc4b7567-9dff-39eb-94ca-91d04b847e43",
                        "entry_id": "92de712e-0021-3d68-b549-706a5aca3b76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of Mercedes-Benz."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "993102be-b6cc-4e2e-b063-52e52d77069b",
                                "sense_id": "bc4b7567-9dff-39eb-94ca-91d04b847e43",
                                "text": "And\nfor those of us with less $$$, one of the BMW 3-series or MB C class should\nsatisfy all needs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09424ab2-8568-4834-8eef-3240fbac8de8",
                                "sense_id": "bc4b7567-9dff-39eb-94ca-91d04b847e43",
                                "text": "Though I'm not an expert, as a long-term MB owner I have read and been\ntold that MB coolant is superior because of its buffering properties. It\nretains a stable pH for longer than the large commercial brands. I used\nto think \"propylene glycol is all the same\" however others have convinced\nme it's cheap insurance to go with original MB coolant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65a7c6c2-533e-4513-a773-eaac68b3cb78",
                                "sense_id": "bc4b7567-9dff-39eb-94ca-91d04b847e43",
                                "text": "Yeah MB still does make inline sixes just low volumes (mainly for\nDaewoo). Apart from the Diesel engines they build for trucks and buses."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa4ac581-2e5f-4158-b621-833a05bd3774",
                                "sense_id": "bc4b7567-9dff-39eb-94ca-91d04b847e43",
                                "text": "I learned part of the reason (at least in USA) started in early 1980's\n(I think 1982) when MB cars started to be built in USA."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "31c576d1-889a-306f-b307-fbb98091a75d",
                        "entry_id": "92de712e-0021-3d68-b549-706a5aca3b76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of Matchbox."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e347f640-5bc2-4b5e-a6be-4c71a9f117d3",
                                "sense_id": "31c576d1-889a-306f-b307-fbb98091a75d",
                                "text": "Just found a new batch of MB: Green Viper #10, New Viper Hardtop #1, Red\nProwler #38, BMW #25, plus several others. MB has really done well in 1997."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c55313a8-ad37-459b-aa8c-fbd1a3df57a7",
                                "sense_id": "31c576d1-889a-306f-b307-fbb98091a75d",
                                "text": "I am looking for the following MB cars, please email me if you have any\nand the price you are asking:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2db4d801-934a-4dc9-8aa2-75a1695d4ac5",
                                "sense_id": "31c576d1-889a-306f-b307-fbb98091a75d",
                                "text": ">Are there any Subaru HW or MB cars, any year???\nNope, nada. I used to own a Subary Legacy myself and was always looking (still\nlooking) for a diecast of the same. No Hotwheels or Matchbox castings have\nbeen made ... yet"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
